    tableWrap.insertAdjacentHTML("afterend",
      "<div id=\"lgd-share-wrap\">"
      + "<a href=\"https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=" + shareText + "\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"lgd-share-btn\" title=\"Share on X\" aria-label=\"Share on X\">" + iconX + "</a>"
      + "<a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/shareArticle?mini=true&url=" + shareUrl + "\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"lgd-share-btn\" title=\"Share on LinkedIn\" aria-label=\"Share on LinkedIn\">" + iconIn + "</a>"
      + "<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/sharer/sharer.php?u=" + shareUrl + "\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"lgd-share-btn\" title=\"Share on Facebook\" aria-label=\"Share on Facebook\">" + iconFb + "</a>"
      + "<a href=\"https://pinterest.com/pin/create/button/?url=" + shareUrl + "\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"lgd-share-btn\" title=\"Save to Pinterest\" aria-label=\"Save to Pinterest\">" + iconPin + "</a>"
      + "<button class=\"lgd-share-btn\" title=\"Copy link\" aria-label=\"Copy link\" onclick=\"lgdCopyLink(this)\">" + iconLink + "</button>"
      + "</div>"
    );

    calloutWrap.insertAdjacentHTML("beforebegin",
      "<span id=\"key-findings\" aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"display:block;height:0;overflow:hidden;\"></span>"
      + buildHistoryHtml(data)
    );

    calloutWrap.innerHTML = "<div style=\"background:#1a1a1a;color:#ffffff;border-radius:6px;padding:20px 24px;line-height:1.7;font-size:0.95rem;\">"
      + "<strong style=\"display:block;margin-bottom:10px;font-size:1rem;color:#ffffff;\">Key Findings: " + data.month + "</strong>"
      + "<p style=\"margin:0 0 14px;color:#c8c8c8;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.6;\">Seven retailers. 251,098 listings. E VS1 Round Excellent IGI.</p>"
      + "<ul style=\"margin:0;padding:0 0 0 18px;color:#ffffff;line-height:1.65;\">"
      + "<li style=\"margin:0 0 9px;\"><strong>Ritani reversed course, raising prices at every tracked weight.</strong> Its 1ct median rose from $223 to $281 per carat (+26%), 1.5ct from $212 to $254 (+20%), and 2ct from $248 to $292 (+18%), the opposite direction from August's decline across the same three cells. The 1ct sample fell from 1,126 stones to 504 and 1.5ct from 1,394 to 975, while Ritani's overall September collection (78,635 rows) was within 5% of August's (81,986), so the sample drop is concentrated in this specific carat/color/clarity/cut cell, not a smaller overall collection.</li>"
      + "<li style=\"margin:0 0 9px;\"><strong>Brilliant Earth's 1.5ct cell dropped 32%, the panel's largest single-cell move this edition.</strong> Its 1.5ct median fell from $1,151 to $784 per carat; by contrast its 1ct median moved -7% ($856 to $796) and 2ct +1% ($1,365 to $1,378). This was checked against the underlying listings (216 distinct URLs, prices $840-$1,810, a normal-looking distribution for the cell) rather than taken as a possible collection artifact.</li>"
      + "<li style=\"margin:0 0 9px;\"><strong>Grown Brilliance held its 1ct and 1.5ct medians exactly flat while its listed inventory fell.</strong> The 1ct sample dropped from 795 to 435 stones (median unchanged at $500/ct) and 1.5ct held at 371 to 376 stones (median unchanged at $648/ct); 2ct rose 3% ($659 to $678/ct) on a smaller sample too, 920 stones to 530. None of the three cells moved by more than 3%, the most stable retailer on the panel this edition despite the inventory swings.</li>"
      + "<li style=\"margin:0 0 9px;\"><strong>Blue Nile's IGI cells returned at 1.5ct and 2ct, retiring the GIA reference row used the last two editions.</strong> Its E VS1 IGI round cells cleared the 30-listing minimum at 1.5ct (n=56, $669/ct) and 2ct (n=54, $820/ct) for the first time since June; 1ct remains thin (n=27). Because Blue Nile's own IGI series is available again for most cells, the separate Blue Nile (GIA) reference row shown in July and August (used only when IGI cells were unpublishable) does not appear this edition; it returns if Blue Nile's IGI cells thin again.</li>"
      + "<li style=\"margin:0 0 9px;\"><strong>VRAI's inventory was completely repriced-flat this cycle, a sharp reversal from August's +76% same-lot jump.</strong> Of 690 listings present in both the August 29 and September 17 collections (matched by product URL), every single one carries an identical price to the cent. VRAI's published cells land at $1,583/ct (1ct, n=36) and a $2,145 median total stone price (1.5ct window, n=92; see the VRAI methodology note on why this cell uses the raw median rather than ppc x weight); its 2ct cell (n=11) remains below the minimum.</li>"
      + "<li style=\"margin:0 0 9px;\"><strong>Clean Origin's 1.5ct cell recovered above the minimum; its 1ct cell has not.</strong> 1.5ct held n=210 this edition (was thin at n=24 in August), publishing at $263/ct; 2ct held roughly flat, $279/ct (n=197) against $278/ct (n=187) in August. The 1ct cell remains thin (n=20, was n=1 in August): still far short of the 30-listing minimum despite the partial recovery elsewhere in the panel.</li>"
      + "<li style=\"margin:0 0 9px;\"><strong>The 1ct Market Median returns after two editions withheld: $571, from Ritani, Grown Brilliance, With Clarity, and Brilliant Earth.</strong> The same four retailers were the only ones with a published 1ct figure in both August and September, so the contributor-eligibility test passes; because August itself withheld its 1ct Market Median, there is no prior published figure to test the move against, so this edition's figure is published as newly re-established rather than compared to a withheld prior value. 1.5ct and 2ct are withheld this edition: Blue Nile's newly-published cells (both weights) and Clean Origin's newly-published 1.5ct cell were not part of either cell's published contributor set in August, so the rule's contributor-eligibility test fails for both, exactly the composition-change case the rule exists to catch. See the Market Median methodology note.</li>"
      + "<li style=\"margin:0;\"><strong>With Clarity's collection was a full capture on all three bands, the first time since June.</strong> All three cells now report a complete count rather than a partial-capture floor: 1ct $642/ct (n=453), 1.5ct $711/ct (n=997, +2.9% from August's disclosed 85%-capture floor of $691), 2ct $736/ct (n=300, +6.1% from $694). Because August's 1.5ct figure was itself a floor, some or all of this edition's 1.5ct increase may reflect the removal of that floor rather than a price move; this index cannot separate the two from the data available.</li>"
      + "</ul></div>";

    var nextEd = nextMonthOf(data.month);
    calloutWrap.insertAdjacentHTML("afterend",
      "<div id=\"lgd-email-wrap\"><h3>Get the " + nextEd + " update</h3>"
      + "<p class=\"lgd-email-sub\">Monthly index delivered to your inbox when new data publishes.</p>"
      + "<form class=\"lgd-email-form\" onsubmit=\"lgdEmailSubmit(event)\">"
      + "<input type=\"email\" placeholder=\"your@email.com\" required aria-label=\"Email address\">"
      + "<button type=\"submit\">Notify me</button></form>"
      + "<p class=\"lgd-email-confirm\">You're on the list.</p></div>"
    );

    var methodHtml = "<h2 style=\"font-size:1rem;font-weight:700;margin:0 0 12px;color:#1a1a1a;\">Methodology</h2><div style=\"font-size:0.9rem;color:#333;line-height:1.7;\">";
    METHODOLOGY.forEach(function (para) { methodHtml += "<p style=\"margin:0 0 12px;color:#333;\">" + para + "</p>"; });
    methodWrap.innerHTML = methodHtml + "</div>";

    // Folds (2026-09-03 redesign): Key Findings bullets and Methodology paragraphs keep their bold
    // lead visible and fold the rest. Post-processing, so the synced KEY_FINDINGS/METHODOLOGY regions stay intact.
    function lgdFold(container, sel, dark) {
      if (!container) return;
      Array.prototype.forEach.call(container.querySelectorAll(sel), function (el) {
        var strong = el.querySelector("strong");
        if (!strong || strong !== el.firstElementChild) return;
        var d = document.createElement("details");
        d.className = "lgd-fold" + (dark ? " lgd-dark" : "");
        var sm = document.createElement("summary");
        sm.innerHTML = strong.innerHTML;
        var body = document.createElement("div");
        body.className = "lgd-fold-body";
        strong.parentNode.removeChild(strong);
        body.innerHTML = el.innerHTML.replace(/^\s+/, "");
        d.appendChild(sm); d.appendChild(body);
        el.parentNode.replaceChild(d, el);
      });
    }
    lgdFold(calloutWrap, "li", true);
    var kfUl = calloutWrap.querySelector("ul");
    if (kfUl) { var kfDiv = document.createElement("div"); kfDiv.id = "lgd-kf-list"; while (kfUl.firstChild) kfDiv.appendChild(kfUl.firstChild); kfUl.parentNode.replaceChild(kfDiv, kfUl); }
    lgdFold(methodWrap, "p", false);

    var nextEdNote = data.next_edition_note || "Updated monthly. Next edition: week of October 26, 2026.";
    footerWrap.innerHTML = "<p style=\"font-size:0.8rem;color:#888;margin:0 0 6px;line-height:1.5;\">" + nextEdNote + "</p>"
      + "<p style=\"font-size:0.78rem;color:#999;margin:0;line-height:1.6;\">Rings.com Lab-Grown Diamond Price Index. &copy; 2026 Rings.com. All rights reserved.</p>";
  }

  window.lgdCopyLink = function (btn) {
    if (navigator.clipboard && navigator.clipboard.writeText) {
      navigator.clipboard.writeText(PAGE_URL).then(function () {
        btn.setAttribute("title", "Copied!");
        setTimeout(function () { btn.setAttribute("title", "Copy link"); }, 2000);
      });
    }
  };

  window.lgdEmailSubmit = function (e) {
    e.preventDefault();
    var form = e.target;
    var input = form.querySelector("input[type=\"email\"]");
    var btn = form.querySelector("button");
    var wrap = document.getElementById("lgd-email-wrap");
    var conf = wrap ? wrap.querySelector(".lgd-email-confirm") : null;
    if (!input || !input.value || !/^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$/.test(input.value)) return;
    btn.textContent = "...";
    btn.disabled = true;
    fetch("https://manage.kmail-lists.com/ajax/subscriptions/subscribe", {
      method: "POST",
      headers: {"Content-Type": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded; charset=utf-8"},
      body: "g=" + encodeURIComponent(KLAVIYO_LIST) + "&email=" + encodeURIComponent(input.value)
    })
    .then(function (res) { return res.json(); })
    .then(function (json) {
      if (json.success) { form.style.display = "none"; if (conf) conf.style.display = "block"; }
      else { btn.textContent = "Notify me"; btn.disabled = false; }
    })
    .catch(function () { btn.textContent = "Notify me"; btn.disabled = false; });
  };

  var fetchData = null, domReady = false;
  function tryRender() {
    if (domReady && fetchData) {
      try { render(fetchData); }
      catch (e) {
        var t = document.getElementById("lgd-table-wrap");
        if (t) t.innerHTML = "<p style=\"padding:16px;color:red;font-family:monospace;\">Render error: " + e.message + "</p>";
      }
    }
  }

  fetch(DATA_URL)
    .then(function (res) { return res.ok ? res.json() : Promise.reject(); })
    .then(function (d) { fetchData = d; tryRender(); })
    .catch(function () { fetchData = FALLBACK; tryRender(); });

  function checkDom() {
    if (document.getElementById("lgd-table-wrap")) {
      if (obs) obs.disconnect();
      domReady = true;
      tryRender();
      return true;
    }
    return false;
  }
  var obs;
  if (!checkDom()) {
    obs = new MutationObserver(function () { checkDom(); });
    obs.observe(document.documentElement, {childList: true, subtree: true});
  }

})();
</script>
{% endif %}
